      "path": "docs/programs/native-interface-component-contract-2026-10-21/README.md",
      "blob": "ea960adb38e0",
      "lines": {
        "8": "Existing `Element`/`ContextDocument` contracts remain intact. A TSX component and Python component may share source fact identities and typed data ports, but are not required to emit identical output trees. The TSX interface host uses the existing `RftsxElement` identity and a separate interactive rendering projection. **Do not create a second general UI IR** or reinterpret model-context blocks as browser/TUI controls.",
        "15": "Optional producer mode: a Python component can emit its validated element or semantic output into an authorized remote stream. The consuming UI host resolves registered known component identities and actions separately. No executable callback serializes to the browser or terminal. Cross-language serialization crosswalk requires strict schema-version checks, `null` semantics, key ordering and error cases. Treat Reactivity as source dependencies, not mandatory server-rendered UI trees.",
        "18": "Portable component shape includes stable ID, typed props, key, declared action IDs and resource bindings; runtime-local action handler registration occurs in TSX interface host, not this Python package. Terminal art styles and browser CSS remain entirely owned by their interface packages.",
        "21": "RC-IF-01: exhaustive Python `Element` versus TSX `RftsxElement` crosswalk; differences and explicit refusal behavior.",
        "24": "RC-IF-04: Python-defined remote component producer opt-in and resolver validation, only once actual Web/TUI hosts are installed consumers.",
        "29": "Current context outputs and recovery/visibility goldens must remain stable. Test source revisions, keyed moves, missing pending resources, denied audience, remote element unsupported IDs, effect declarations during failed render, streamed provisional text and malformed action references. No Github CI; use Forge and package-local installed consumer tests on default branch master."
      }
    },
